# PantryPal MVP 

## 1. Project Overview

We're building an ingredient-first recipe matcher that answers one core question: "What can I cook right now?" Users sign up, build their pantry once, then instantly see recipes ranked by match quality—with recipes using the most of their ingredients appearing first. The magic happens through intelligent matching powered by our mock recipe database, with the front end focusing on delightful UX, pantry persistence, and clear visualization of what users have versus what they need. Success is measured by how quickly users go from "random ingredients" to "I know what to cook"—making the gap between inspiration and action as short as possible.

This is a front-end-only first approach. Do not implement any back-end functionality.

## 2. User Types and Permissions

**All Users (Signed-In)**
- Must create an account to use the app via Supabase Auth (email/password)
- Can search unlimited recipes using their pantry or custom ingredient input
- Access to full mock recipe catalog
- Can save and manage their pantry (persists across sessions)
- Can save unlimited favorite recipes
- Can filter favorites by cookability based on current pantry
- All saved data protected by Row Level Security

**Permission Matrix**
| Feature | Available |
|---------|-----------|
| Search recipes by ingredients | ✅ |
| View recipe details | ✅ |
| Autocomplete ingredients | ✅ |
| Save and manage pantry | ✅ |
| Save and manage favorites | ✅ |
| Filter favorites by cookability | ✅ |

